<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15507" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ē-lixus</span></b> , a, um,
		adj., lix, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>thoroughly boiled</i>, <i>boiled</i>, <i>seethed.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, Varr. ap. <i><span class="en">Non.
				62, 14</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 20, 6, 23, § 54</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Hor.
				S. 2, 2, 74</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Juv. 3, 294</span></i>; <i><span class="en">13, 85</span></i>; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">the punning use of the word,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Poen. 1, 2, 67</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Most. 5, 1,
			66</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, qs. sodden, i. e., <i>soaked</i>, <i>wet through</i>: calcei, Varr.
			ap. <i><span class="en">Non. 48, 27</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">balneator,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. 3,
					7</span></i>
			: nates, i. e. <i>quite flabby</i> after the
			bath, <i><span class="en">Pers.
				4, 40</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
